---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const repo = 'https://github.com/LiamLiamFitzgerald/cs4421-astro-blog';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About · ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="What this project is and how it is built." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p>
				This site is my project for <strong>CS4421 DevOps</strong> at the University of Limerick. The
				Catan scoreboard is the product, but the point of the project is the engineering around it:
				code that stays easy to change, checks that catch mistakes before they merge, and a deploy
				that can be repeated, observed and rolled back.
			</p>

			<h2>What happens on every pull request</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Commit messages are checked against Conventional Commits.</li>
				<li>Lint, type checks and architecture rules run.</li>
				<li>Unit, property-based and end-to-end browser tests run.</li>
				<li>The site, the container image and the AWS infrastructure are built and tested.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Branches follow GitFlow: features merge into <code>develop</code> through pull requests, and
				releases go to <code>main</code>, where release-please writes the changelog and version tag.
				Mutation testing runs weekly to check that the tests actually catch bugs.
			</p>

			<h2>Read more</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><a href={`${repo}/blob/develop/docs/architecture.md`}>Architecture overview</a></li>
				<li><a href={`${repo}/tree/develop/docs/adr`}>Architecture decision records</a></li>
				<li><a href={`${repo}/blob/develop/docs/handbook.md`}>Developer handbook</a></li>
				<li><a href={repo}>Source code</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>Built by Liam Fitzgerald.</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
